// Emulation sessions over a program's code (api_minor 12, feature
// "emulator"; docs/emulator.md). A session runs the program's machine code
// in revkit's p-code emulator: registers, memory written over the loaded
// image, breakpoints and a bounded trace.
//
// Session state is the caller's, not a fact about the binary: nothing is
// asserted, no revision is made, and other clients don't see it unless
// they hold the session id. Sessions are bounded in steps and memory, each
// call in time, and are closed after a period without use.

